opencode2-bin packages the OpenCode 2.0 release line, an open source AI
coding agent for the terminal.

This package ships the self-contained binary built by upstream and
installs it as `opencode`. Upstream publishes the 2.0 line only to the
npm registry as `@opencode/cli-linux-x64`; there is no GitHub release
tarball for it, so this package repacks that npm artifact.

The binary is compiled with Bun and is self-contained (no runtime
dependencies). The default build targets glibc x86_64 with AVX2. On a
CPU without AVX2, use the `-baseline` variant instead.

OpenCode v1 and v2 use the same configuration and state directories
(`~/.config/opencode`, `~/.local/share/opencode`), and both the v1
`opencode-bin` package and this one install the binary as `opencode`.
The two packages therefore conflict; install one or the other, not both,
and back up your configuration before switching versions.

Homepage: https://opencode.ai
